    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "With no lands in hand, the player needs to enable Metalcraft (3 artifacts) to activate Mox Opal for mana. The correct sequence is to cast Mox Opal first, then Mishra's Bauble, then Engineered Explosives (for X=0) to reach Metalcraft and have access to mana. By casting Mishra's Bauble first, nothing changes functionally since all three zero-cost artifacts will be cast this turn anyway, BUT casting Mox Opal first is strictly better because if the opponent has any instant-speed interaction (e.g., a response that would prevent further casting), you want your mana source on the battlefield first. Additionally, casting Mishra's Bauble first and sacrificing it won't draw a card until next upkeep, so it doesn't help find a land this turn. The order matters slightly - Mox Opal should come down first as a general sequencing principle of deploying mana sources before other spells. However, since all three will likely resolve this turn with no opponent interaction possible (it's the main phase and opponent has no board), the practical impact is minimal.",
      "action_taken": "Cast Mishra's Bauble first before Mox Opal",
      "better_line": "Cast Mox Opal first, then Mishra's Bauble, then Engineered Explosives for X=0 to enable Metalcraft immediately and have mana available as early as possible",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 4,
