      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Targeting yourself with Mishra's Bauble is almost always worse than targeting your opponent. Looking at your own top card gives you marginal information (you'll draw it next turn regardless), while looking at the opponent's top card gives you valuable information about what they're planning, which is especially useful when you're holding Metallic Rebuke as a counterspell. Knowing what the opponent will draw helps you decide whether to hold up countermagic or deploy threats.",
      "action_taken": "Targeted themselves with Mishra's Bauble to look at their own top card.",
      "better_line": "Target the opponent (Gem3F Villain) with Mishra's Bauble to see their top card, gaining information about their next draw to better plan counterspell usage with Metallic Rebuke.",
