      "description": "With 4 artifacts on board (Mox Opal, Engineered Explosives, Shadowspear, and the tapped Spirebluff Canal is a land not artifact), Mox Opal has Metalcraft active (Mox Opal, Engineered Explosives, Shadowspear = 3 artifacts). Casting Pinnacle Emissary for its Warp cost of {U/R} would only cost 1 mana, deploying a 3/3 that generates tokens when artifact spells are cast. It would exile at end step but could be recast later. However, the player has Metallic Rebuke in hand and the opponent has only 1 tapped land, so holding up countermagic isn't critical this turn. Warping out Pinnacle Emissary for just 1 mana while still having mana available for Rebuke (with Improvise from artifacts) could have been a strong tempo play - getting a 3/3 attacker and setting up future recasts from exile.",
