      "severity": "major",
      "description": "Overlord of the Balemurk is a 5/5 that mills four cards on ETB and returns a creature or planeswalker from graveyard to hand. Against a Living End deck with Street Wraith, Subtlety, Endurance, and Generous Ent already in the graveyard, this is devastating — it will mill more creatures into the graveyard (fueling a future Living End) and immediately recur a powerful creature like Endurance or Subtlety. The opponent cast it for its full cost ({3}{B}{B}), meaning it enters as a 5/5 creature. With Metallic Rebuke available and Improvise making it cost only {U} (tap Engineered Explosives and Shadowspear as artifacts, plus Steam Vents or Spirebluff Canal for {U}), this was a free counter that should have been used on a must-answer threat. The opponent would need to pay {3} to avoid the counter, which on turn 3 with all lands tapped they cannot do.",
